                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Update 7/23/18[/b]\nWas one of the first purchasers of this game and still 4 years later I get great joy to pop this little gem open and destroy things. \n\n\n[b]Previously[/b]\n\nPixel Star is an addicting and fun shoot em up where progression is chaos! If you like to blow up ALL things then get this! You won't be disappointed. But if you are looking for a fast 100% game this may not be the one for you unless you are just that super awesome. However i find  it a welcome change with the challenge for a few achievements [i](or super awesome blind luck)[/i] versus some other games handed achievements, linear play or progressive killing grind. \n\nWhen you start the game you get to customize three aspects of your ship. The Hull, Utility and Secondary weapon. They all have their uses and obviously it will be what fits your play style. \nI really loved picking the magnet in Utility to have all the asteroids and enemies get sucked into one spot so i could blow them up, and use the rainbow cannon as my Secondary to make it that much quicker. In early game this will net you a lot of power ups quickly. Magnet also worked great to toss out when trying to escape. :D\n\nHere are the options for a quick glance. \n[list]\n[*]Hull[list]\n [*]Invulnerability \n [*]Regenerate secondary ammo \n [*]Faster utility recharge \n[/list][/list]\n[list]\n[*]Utility [list] \n [*]Teleportation drive \n [*]Deflection mirrors \n [*]Ultra magnet \n [*]Force blaster \n [*]Liquid plasma \n [*]Slow time \n[/list][/list]\n[list]\n[*]Secondary [list]\n [*]Homing missiles \n [*]Timed bombs \n [*]Attack drones \n [*]Static generator \n [*]Gatling gun \n [*]Rainbow cannon \n[/list][/list]\n\nOnce you get into the game you will see the controls as part of the background and begin your killing. There are many many enemies, and a first they will seem easy and silly and then as you progress you will find some of them are rather tricky and can one shot you if you are not careful. \n\nThere are also a lot of power ups you can obtain. Lasers is the best, they have a red circle and they stack up making your default attack more powerful with a lot more laser beams. Then there are also Barrage which add projectiles to your attack. It really does get chaotic! There are also Repair that will stack up giving you the ability to take more damage, and last longer of course. There are Shield power ups which do exactly that, shield your ship from attacks. There are also little drones that float around your ship and help attack. The rapid fire is a short burst, great to snag before a boss. There are also Flare that float around your ship and if an enemy gets too close they will be destroyed, otherwise they sort of act like another shield around you. Ammo of course for your secondary weapon and a Secondary Power to make it stronger. Then there is a Turbo that will boost your speed for a short time, and a few are needed in a row to obtain an achievement. \nIn addition there is a Civilian bounty on screen, a yellow exclamation, that you don't want to destroy as flying into it will give a power up.",
